<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Minab</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Minab is a city in Hormozgan Province in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, on the Minab River near the Strait of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hormuz">Hormuz</a>. It lies near the site of Old Hormuz, the mainland port and capital of the kingdom of Hormuz until around 1300, when raids drove its king to move to the island of Jarun. The area is known for its date palms and its Thursday market.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/minab.jpg" alt="Minab" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: نادر مظلومی · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BANDAR_ABBAS_(3)_%D8%AF%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%86%D9%85%D8%A7%DB%8C%DB%8C_%D8%A7%D8%B2_%D8%B4%D9%87%D8%B1_%D9%85%DB%8C%D9%86%D8%A7%D8%A8_%D8%AF%D8%B1_%D9%87%D8%B1%D9%85%D8%B2%DA%AF%D8%A7%D9%86.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
